      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin (850 mg per dose, three times daily). Extended-release is capped at 2,000 mg/day. At this dose the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity is significant, even with normal renal function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the max)\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals\n- **Another dose**, such as 500 mg or 1,000 mg per dose\n\nIf 1,700 mg three times daily is what you want, please confirm it and I'll enter it with a note saying it was intentional. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
